    procedure: "MTP & Abortion",
    keywords: ["medical-abortion-pills-india-2026", "Medical Abortion Pills in India 2026 — How They Work, Cost, "],
    body: 'Medical abortion using pills is the safest and least invasive method for terminating an early pregnancy. Here is everything you need to know about medical abortion in India 2026.\n\nWhat Are Abortion Pills?\n\nMedical abortion uses two medicines — mifepristone and misoprostol. Mifepristone blocks the hormone progesterone that is needed to continue the pregnancy. Misoprostol is taken 24 to 48 hours later and causes the uterus to contract and expel the pregnancy. The process is similar to an early miscarriage.\n\nMedical abortion is available up to 9 weeks (63 days) of pregnancy in India. Beyond 9 weeks surgical abortion is recommended for safety and completeness.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nHow Effective Are Abortion Pills?\n\nMedical abortion is over 95% effective up to 7 weeks. Effectiveness decreases slightly to 93 to 95% between 7 and 9 weeks. If medical abortion is incomplete a surgical procedure (S&E or D&C) can complete the process. MySurgery always arranges a 2-week follow-up ultrasound to confirm complete termination.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Meenakshi Ahuja (MD (OBG), FICOG) — 30 years of experience — practices at Fortis La Femme, Delhi. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 to book a consultation with Dr. Meenakshi Ahuja or a similar expert in your city.\n\nCost of Abortion Pills in India 2026\n\nMedical abortion in India costs Rs 3,000 to Rs 8,000. This includes the doctor consultation, ultrasound to confirm gestational age, the medicines, and the follow-up. Cost varies by city — Delhi and Mumbai are at the higher end, smaller cities are cheaper. MySurgery provides transparent pricing with no hidden charges.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nAre Abortion Pills Available Online in India?\n\nNo. Taking abortion pills without medical supervision is dangerous and illegal. An ultrasound is essential before taking the pills to confirm gestational age and rule out ectopic pregnancy. An ectopic pregnancy is a life-threatening emergency and must not be treated with pills.\n\nAlways consult a registered gynaecologist. MySurgery connects you with registered doctors who prescribe and supervise medical abortion safely and legally.\n\nWhat Happens After Taking Abortion Pills?\n\nCramping and bleeding begin within 1 to 4 hours of taking misoprostol. Heavy bleeding with clots is normal and confirms the process is working. Bleeding slows to a lighter flow over 1 to 2 weeks. A follow-up ultrasound at 2 weeks confirms complete termination. Menstrual cycle returns in 4 to 6 weeks.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050',
