    authorTitle: "MS (OBG), FICOG, 24 years experience, Max Hospital Delhi",
    category: "Urology",
    readTime: "8 min read",
    quickAnswer: 'D&C (Dilation and Curettage) surgery costs Rs 8,000 to Rs 25,000 in India depending on city and hospital. The procedure takes 15 to 20 minutes under anaesthesia with same-day discharge. It is used for abortion, miscarriage management, and uterine investigation.',
    procedure: "Circumcision (Laser/ZSR)",
    keywords: ["dnc-surgery-cost-india-2026", "D&C Surgery Cost in India 2026 — Dilation and Curettage Comp"],
    body: 'D&C (Dilation and Curettage) is a common gynaecological procedure used for abortion, incomplete miscarriage management, and uterine investigation. Here is a complete guide to D&C in India 2026.\n\nWhat Is D&C?\n\nD&C involves two steps. Dilation: the cervix is gently widened using dilators. Curettage: a curette (a thin, spoon-shaped instrument) is used to scrape or suction out the uterine lining. The procedure takes 15 to 20 minutes under local or general anaesthesia.\n\nD&C for Abortion\n\nD&C is used for surgical abortion from 12 to 20 weeks of pregnancy. Beyond 12 weeks, suction evacuation (S&E) is often combined with D&C for complete and safe termination.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nD&C Cost in India 2026\n\nD&C surgery costs Rs 8,000 to Rs 25,000 in India depending on city, hospital, and gestational age. Delhi and Mumbai: Rs 12,000 to Rs 22,000. Bangalore and Chennai: Rs 10,000 to Rs 20,000. Tier-2 cities: Rs 8,000 to Rs 15,000.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Geeta Chadha (MS (OBG), FICOG) — 24 years of experience — practices at Max Hospital, Delhi. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 to book a consultation with Dr. Geeta Chadha or a similar expert in your city.\n\nIs D&C Safe?\n\nYes. D&C performed by a qualified gynaecologist at a registered hospital is a safe procedure. Complication rates are below 1%. Potential but rare risks include uterine perforation, infection, and Asherman syndrome (uterine scarring). These risks are extremely rare with an experienced doctor.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nD&C vs S&E — Which Is Better for Abortion?\n\nFor terminations up to 12 weeks, Suction and Evacuation (S&E or MVA) is preferred over sharp curettage (D&C) because it causes less trauma to the uterine lining. For second trimester terminations (12 to 20 weeks), a combination of medical preparation and surgical evacuation is used.\n\nRecovery After D&C\n\nSame-day discharge. Mild cramping for 1 to 2 days. Light bleeding for up to 2 weeks. Normal activities resume in 1 to 2 days. Avoid intercourse for 2 to 4 weeks. Follow-up ultrasound at 2 weeks to confirm complete evacuation.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050',
