    body: 'Understanding what to expect after MTP helps you recover confidently. Here is a complete day-by-day guide to MTP recovery.\n\nImmediately After MTP (First Few Hours)\n\nAfter surgical S&E or D&C you will rest in a recovery room for 1 to 2 hours. You may feel mild to moderate cramping similar to period pain. Slight dizziness from anaesthesia is normal and passes quickly. You are allowed to eat and drink normally after the procedure. You can go home the same day with a trusted companion.\n\nDay 1 to 3 After MTP\n\nMild to moderate cramping is normal and managed well with ibuprofen or paracetamol. Light to moderate bleeding is expected. You can walk, eat normally, and do light activities. Avoid heavy lifting, exercise, and intercourse. Take prescribed antibiotics and medications exactly as directed.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nWeek 1 to 2 After MTP\n\nBleeding gradually reduces from moderate to light spotting. Cramping significantly decreases after day 3. Most people return to desk work and normal routine within 1 to 2 days. Avoid swimming and baths (showers are fine) for 2 weeks.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Rekha Wadhwani (MS (OBG)) — 19 years of experience — practices at Medanta, Gurugram. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 to book a consultation with Dr. Rekha Wadhwani or a similar expert in your city.\n\nFollow-Up Ultrasound at 2 Weeks\n\nA follow-up ultrasound at 2 weeks is very important to confirm complete termination. If anything remains in the uterus it can be treated with a simple procedure. MySurgery arranges your follow-up ultrasound and doctor review as part of the care package.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nEmotional Recovery After MTP\n\nFeelings after MTP vary widely — relief, sadness, grief, or a mix of emotions are all completely normal. There is no right or wrong way to feel. If you experience prolonged sadness or anxiety speak to your doctor or a counsellor. MySurgery can connect you with supportive counselling services if needed.\n\nWhen Menstruation Returns\n\nYour menstrual cycle typically returns 4 to 6 weeks after MTP. The first period may be heavier or lighter than usual. Regular cycles return within 2 to 3 cycles. Fertility returns immediately — use contraception immediately if you do not want to become pregnant again.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050',
