    readTime: "8 min read",
    quickAnswer: 'Survivors of rape or sexual assault can terminate pregnancy up to 24 weeks in India under the MTP Act 2021. No police report is required for MTP. No husband or family permission is needed. The procedure is completely confidential and free at government hospitals.',
    procedure: "MTP & Abortion",
    keywords: ["abortion-after-rape-india-legal-rights", "Abortion After Rape in India — Your Legal Rights Under MTP A"],
    body: "The Medical Termination of Pregnancy Act India 2021 provides special protection for survivors of sexual assault. Here is a clear guide to your rights.\n\nYour Rights as a Survivor\n\nUnder the MTP Act 2021, survivors of rape and sexual assault can terminate pregnancy up to 24 weeks with one registered doctor approval. This is one of the most important expansions in the 2021 amendment. You do not need a police FIR or any legal documentation to access MTP. You do not need a family member's consent or permission. Only your own informed consent is required.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nConfidentiality for Survivors\n\nDoctors are legally prohibited from disclosing your identity or details to anyone including police or your family without your explicit consent. MySurgery provides absolute confidentiality and has female care coordinators and female doctors available for survivors.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Meenakshi Ahuja (MD (OBG), FICOG) — 30 years of experience — practices at Fortis La Femme, Delhi. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 to book a consultation with Dr. Meenakshi Ahuja or a similar expert in your city.\n\nFree MTP at Government Hospitals\n\nSurvivors of sexual assault are entitled to free MTP at all government hospitals in India. Many government hospitals have dedicated one-stop crisis centres (OSCCs) that provide medical care, counselling, and legal support for survivors.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nMySurgery's Support for Survivors\n\nMySurgery provides compassionate, non-judgmental support for survivors. Our female care coordinators will speak with you in complete confidence. We can arrange priority appointments, female doctors, and counselling referrals. We will never pressurize you or make you feel judged.\n\nIf you or someone you know needs help please call us immediately at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us. We are here for you.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050",
