    body: "Whether health insurance covers MTP in India is a common question. The answer depends on the reason for MTP and the specific insurance policy.\n\nWhen Is MTP Covered by Insurance?\n\nSome health insurance policies cover MTP when it is medically indicated. Covered situations may include: foetal abnormalities detected on anomaly scan, medical risk to the mother's life, incomplete miscarriage requiring D&C, and management of ectopic pregnancy.\n\nWhen Is MTP NOT Covered?\n\nMost policies do not cover: elective MTP for an unwanted pregnancy, MTP due to contraceptive failure without medical indication, second trimester termination for social reasons.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nHow to Check Your Insurance Coverage\n\nRead your policy document carefully — look for exclusions related to pregnancy termination. Call your insurance company helpline and ask specifically about MTP coverage. Check if your employer's group insurance has different terms — some corporate policies are more comprehensive.\n\nMySurgery can help you check your insurance coverage and understand what is and is not covered for your specific situation.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Sunita Varma (MS (OBG), Fellowship Laparoscopic Gynaecology) — 20 years of experience — practices at Medanta Lucknow, Lucknow. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 to book a consultation with Dr. Sunita Varma or a similar expert in your city.\n\nMTP Without Insurance — Payment Options\n\nMTP is relatively affordable in India especially in Tier-2 cities. For patients without insurance coverage MySurgery offers transparent pricing with no hidden charges. EMI options are available through healthcare finance companies for procedures above Rs 10,000.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nConfidentiality and Insurance Claims\n\nIf you are filing an insurance claim for MTP, the claim will typically require a doctor's note with a medical reason. This is kept between you and your insurance company. MySurgery can help you with the documentation for eligible claims while maintaining complete confidentiality.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050",
