    category: "Gynecology",
    readTime: "8 min read",
    quickAnswer: 'Girls under 18 can get an abortion in India up to 24 weeks under the MTP Act 2021. Parental consent may be required for minors but a legal guardian can also provide consent. Complete confidentiality is maintained. Free services are available at government hospitals.',
    procedure: "MTP & Abortion",
    keywords: ["mtp-abortion-for-minors-india", "Abortion for Minors in India — Legal Rights and Access"],
    body: "Unplanned pregnancy in minors is a sensitive and urgent situation. Here is everything you need to know about abortion rights for girls under 18 in India.\n\nLegal Rights of Minors Under MTP Act 2021\n\nThe MTP Act 2021 explicitly includes minors as a special category who can terminate pregnancy up to 24 weeks (compared to 20 weeks for adult women in general circumstances). This reflects recognition of the special vulnerability and needs of minors in such situations.\n\nConsent Requirements for Minors\n\nFor girls under 18, the guardian's written consent is required under the MTP Act (since minors cannot give legally valid informed consent independently). However the 2021 amendment and subsequent legal interpretations have evolved to protect minors' privacy — doctors can help navigate this with sensitivity.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nFree Services for Minors\n\nAll government hospitals in India must provide free MTP services for minors under 18. This includes consultation, procedure, medications, and post-procedure care. Private hospitals and clinics also have reduced-cost or subsidised services for minors in many states.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Meenakshi Ahuja (MD (OBG), FICOG) — 30 years of experience — practices at Fortis La Femme, Delhi. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 to book a consultation with Dr. Meenakshi Ahuja or a similar expert in your city.\n\nConfidentiality for Minors\n\nMySurgery understands the extreme sensitivity of this situation. Our female care coordinators handle all minor cases with the highest level of confidentiality and compassion. We can also connect minors with legal aid organisations and NGOs that specialise in supporting young women in such situations.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050\n\nImportant Note on POCSO\n\nIf the pregnancy is a result of sexual abuse by an adult the doctor is legally required to report it under the POCSO Act. This is a child protection law and is different from the MTP process. MySurgery's doctors will handle this sensitively and explain the process clearly.\n\nIf you or someone you know is a minor needing MTP support please call MySurgery at 8588807050 immediately. Our female counsellors are available and will provide compassionate, judgment-free support.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588807050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588807050",
